course: dictionary
lesson: 2043
title: One word, more than one meaning
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The context, meaning the words and sentences around them, tells you which meaning you need. «They meet in a parliament — in the United States it is called Congress — where they argue about ideas and vote on new laws.» Here Congress is a group of people who make laws, because they argue and vote on laws.
explain: Now read this: «In 1815 the Congress of Vienna redrew the map of Europe.» Redrawing a map is not a job for lawmakers. Countries sent their representatives to a big, formal meeting, so Congress means a large meeting here. Ask yourself: which meaning fits the sentence?
explain: The words around a word can also give you clues. «Whips try to make their party's MPs vote together; an MP who votes against their own party is called a rebel, and it happens in Congress too.» Whips, party, vote and rebel all point to politics, so Congress here is a place where politicians vote on laws.
fact: Context means the words and sentences around a word.
fact: «Congress» means the group of people elected to make laws in the USA, made up of the Senate and the House of Representatives.
fact: «Congress» can also mean a large formal meeting of representatives from many groups or countries, such as a medical congress.
fact: Some other countries have a law-making body that can also be called a congress.
fact: A capital C in «Congress» usually names the special law-making body of the USA.
exercise: «They meet in a parliament — in the United States it is called Congress — where they argue about ideas and vote on new laws.» In this sentence, what is Congress? | A kind of castle | A big meal for many guests | A type of racing bike | *A group of people who make laws
exercise: «In 1815 the Congress of Vienna redrew the map of Europe.» What kind of meeting was the Congress of Vienna? | A family picnic in the park | A sports match between two teams | *A large formal meeting of representatives from many countries
exercise: Which word in «Whips try to make their party's MPs vote together» hints that Congress is about voting? | Whips | MPs | party's | *vote
test: «Napoleon's empire at its height controlled most of western and central Europe, and after his defeat the Congress of Vienna redrew the map in 1815.» Does congress here mean a group of lawmakers or a big formal meeting? | A school club | Lawmakers in one country | A sports team | *A big formal meeting of countries' representatives
test: Tom says Congress always means a big meeting of countries. What is the best answer? | Yes, it means a sports match | No, it is a kind of bird | Yes, it always means a meeting of countries | *No, in the USA it is the group that makes laws
exam: Why is the C in «Congress» a capital letter in «in the United States it is called Congress»? | It is a spelling mistake | It shows the word is angry | It starts a new sentence | *It names one special body, the law-making group of the USA
